{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\n`tests/unit/test_review_bot.py::test_shutdown_drains_an_in_flight_reconciler_review` fails intermittently in CI's `pytest (ubuntu-latest, py3.12)` cell:\n\n```\nAssertionError: the reconciler's review never fired within 3.0s — the probe is not wired\nassert []\ntests/unit/test_review_bot.py:981\n```\n\n`_await_probe` (`tests/unit/test_review_bot.py:966-981`) polls a worker-thread probe against a fixed 3.0 s wall-clock cap.\n\n## Evidence (measured 2026-11-09, corrected 2026-11-10)\n\n- 1 confirmed failure: run 42742825985 (2026-11-10 02:26 UTC = 2026-11-09 18:26 PST, Gerrit change 3341, which only edits eval-spec `model:` lines and one evidence-kind test). Run 41638314556 (cited originally) did not fail this test; it logged only a slow-fixture timing warning on Windows.\n- The `Errno 98 address already in use` in that run comes from `test_audit_serve::test_await_listening_reports_a_server_that_cannot_bind`, which binds a busy port on purpose. It is unrelated.\n- Not reproduced unaided locally: 0 of 30 isolated runs, 0 of 6 whole-file `-n 4` runs, 0 of 40 xdist repeats on a loaded host.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed; evidence in the ROOT CAUSE comment)\n\nThe fixed 3.0 s readiness cap covers the reconciler's startup work before `review_and_vote` (SQLite WAL setup and `clear_voted` on the loop thread, the cursor read, executor hops). On a contended runner that work can exceed 3 s, and the assertion then misreports a slow start as an unwired probe. A 3.5 s stall injected before the review reproduces CI's exact signature; a 2.5 s stall passes. Production code is not implicated.\n\n## Fix\n\n`_await_probe`'s cap becomes a 20 s hang-guard for all 9 call sites. It returns as soon as the probe fires, so passing runs get no slower. The misattributing message is corrected, and the outer `wait_for` bounds are raised above the cap plus the drain. Change 3343.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A deterministic reproduction of the CI failure signature exists and is recorded on this ticket.\n- [x] The root cause is confirmed by an experiment that distinguishes it from the competing hypotheses (low disk, startup-binding error, lock leak, in-flight stall).\n- [x] `test_shutdown_drains_an_in_flight_reconciler_review` passes when the pre-review startup stalls 3.5 s and 8 s (which failed before the fix).\n- [x] The fix lands on main through Gerrit at LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, and `make verify` passed on the fix commit before the push."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794368253255245205,"uuid":"d88f8f48-3bcc-41e3-bbf6-0c8d30efad19"}